    "note": "Read from the sheet. The pass element A4Q12 (on A4, wired through E4-E7: E4 YEL its output, E5 GRN, E6 BLU, E7 VIO its drive) delivers the 10 V onto E4; CR6 (12 V zener) clamps that node to the supply common, U1 runs from it (pin 7), and R62 2.7 ohm carries it to the 10 V HI bus node that leaves on E23 (10V HI, the force lead). Off that bus node R63 2.7 ohm feeds the CR2 anode / C2 / CR8 node, CR8 (12 V zener) clamping it to common. Two more '10V HI' wires come back from the front-panel post: E24 is the sense line -- the top of the R2 4.22 K / R3 10 K divider (C15 0.22 uF to R24 10 ohm to common) whose tap is U1's - input, the top of R4 1.27 K which feeds the zener half of U2, and one end of R26 51 -- and E25 is the other end of R26, from which R7 6.2 K goes to the Ref-Amp's base and on down R8 11.42 K (TP3), R11, R10 (TP4), the calibration ladder and R19 / R18 / R20 to LO (E26). U2's zener anode sits on the reference common (with R1 / C3 and R3); its transistor's emitter is the zener cathode, its base is the R7 / R8 tap, and its collector is loaded by R5 from the bias node TP2 and is U1's + input; C14 180 pF sits across U1's inputs and C3 1 uF + R1 200 shunt the + input to the reference common. U1's output goes through CR1 (5.2 V zener, cathode on E7) to E7 -- Q1's base -- and Q1 / Q2 drive A4Q12 (§3-19: U1 drives the series pass element Q1, A4Q12; Q2 provides current limiting). The bias node TP1 is fed from +18.6 V (E8) by CR5 (current-regulator diode) in parallel with R9 and held by CR2 (6.4 V compensated zener) one zener above the CR8 node, C2 across CR2; R60 and R6 (both SEL) drop it to TP2 and R5. Q5 is drawn with base and emitter tied to the U2 emitter/zener node and its collector on the U2 base line -- a transistor used as a low-leakage diode across the Ref-Amp's base-emitter, C16 0.047 uF in parallel. The board has two commons: the reference common (R1 / C3, R3, U2 zener anode, C17, a ground symbol; wired to the LO post by E27) and the supply common (E3 ORN to A4 -REF / COMMON; U1 pin 4, R25 / C4, R24 / C15, CR6 and CR8 anodes, a ground symbol; wired to the LO post by E28), joined on the board by R64 51 in parallel with CR7 (anode on the supply common). The 1 V chain hangs from the E33 10V HI wire: (R58 200 1V ADJ + R56 1 K) in parallel with R54 35 to TP13, then R53 + R52 (SEL, in series) shunted by R48 35 down to TP14, R46 8.9 K to E35 (1V HI) and R44 1 K to LO (E36). The 1.018 V chain: (R57 350 + R59 200 1.018V ADJ) in parallel with R55 35 to TP12, R50 + R51 (SEL) shunted by R49 35 to TP11, R47 8.7 K to E34 (1.018V HI) and R45 1 K to LO (E36). All of the ref-amp, error-amp, pass-drive, bias, output and divider parts are starred in Table 5-6.",
