    "note": "§3-24 in the manual's words: thermistors RT1, series connected RT2, and RT3 are connected in a bridge configuration with R28 and R29 and are located inside the oven; U3 buffers the bridge output and drives differential amplifier/integrator U5 which drives the oven driver and output transistors (A4Q13, A4Q14) and subsequently the oven heaters; U4 shapes the overall loop frequency response. Read from the sheet, the designators differ: the two series thermistors under the OVEN bracket are RT3 and RT4 (10 K at 25 C, oven-assembly parts -- Table 5-1's RT1 in 1983, RT3/RT4 from Errata Change #7), RT1 (10 K, an A5 part) is the bridge's return leg to E2, and RT2 (the other A5 thermistor of Table 5-6) is the front-panel OVEN TEMP THERMISTOR between E21 and E22, which takes no part in the loop. Q3 and Q4 (2N3906 PNP, emitters through R21 SEL and R27 10 K to E9) are a current mirror sourcing from the +BRIDGE rail: Q4's base is tied to its own collector and Q3's base to that node (read at 600 dpi), so R27 sets the reference current and Q3 mirrors it scaled by R27 / R21 -- Q3 into the bridge node TP7 (RT3 leg, R22 17.4 K, CR3), Q4 through R28 7.5 K into the U3B input node. From TP7 the thermistor path is RT3 -> midpoint (TP8/TP9) -> RT4 -> TP10 -> RT1 -> E2, with R22 across RT3 + RT4. TP7 itself is U3A's + input (pin 3), with C7 4700 pF from it to E2 (600 dpi: the junction dot is on the CR3 anode and one vertical drops from it to the pin-3 line and through C7; the CR3 / CR4 junction connects to nothing else). CR3 -> CR4 in series run from TP7 to the other bridge node -- CR4 cathode / R28 / R29 / C5 0.22 uF, U3B's + input (pin 5) -- so they act as a clamp that limits how far the thermistor node can rise above the R28 / R29 node (a reading of the sheet; the manual does not describe the two diodes). U3 (LM358) runs from E9 (pin 8) to E1 (pin 4, BRN, -TEMP REG); both halves are drawn as followers. U5 (LM308H) takes U3B's output (pin 7) on its + input and U3A's output (pin 1) through R30 2.15 K on its - input, with R31 1 K, R32 6.2 M, R33 5.1 M, R34 2.4 M and C8 5 uF forming the integrator, C13 100 pF from its compensation pin 8 to E11, R61 1 M from the + input to its V+; U5 runs from +18.6 V (E8, pin 7) to -2 V (E11 BRN, pin 4; A4 P2-27) and its output leaves through R37 1 K on E10 (BLK) as HEAT DRIVE to A4 R26 / Q13. U4 (LM308H, pin 7 on E9, pin 4 on the E1 return, with C12 100 pF from its compensation pin 8 to that node and R23 51 from it to a ground symbol) is the loop-shaping stage: its + input (pin 3) takes the bridge signal through R38 51 K from the U3B output line and, through C10 4 uF, the U5 output through C9 0.47 uF in parallel with R36 + R35 (27 M each); its - input (pin 2) takes the same U3B output line through R39 51 K and its own output through R40 10 K from the R41 6.8 M / C11 270 pF feedback; its output goes through R42 51 K into U5's - input. C6 0.22 uF bypasses E9 to E2. Errata Change #7 adds a 58 C thermal fuse F2 (final assembly) on top of the reference module that interrupts the +18.6 V to the oven heater and to the A4 latch.",
