    "note": "§3-4: the Regulator converts the 32 V to 18.5 V dc which powers the Oven Controller and the Reference (§3-13 and Figure 8-1 print 18.6 V). On A5 the raw +18.6 V arrives on E8 (GRA) only and feeds two things: the Ref-Amp bias node through CR5 / R9, and U5's V+ (pin 7). The E8 line ends at the CR5 / R9 node; the 10 V HI bus drawn just above it is a separate segment (checked at 600 dpi). The +BRIDGE rail on E9 (WHT) is the same 18.6 V after A4 Q5, the voltage monitor's switch (§3-16), and carries everything else in the oven controller: Q3 / Q4 through R21 / R27, U3 pin 8, U4 pin 7. E11 (BRN) is U5's negative supply, lettered -2 V on Figure 8-4's P2-27 (see the caveat about Figure 8-1). The three returns are separate wires that A4 straps together at its COMMON node (P2 pins 2, 3, 4 and 5, TP2 on A4): E1 for U3 and U4, E2 for the thermistor bridge and its capacitors, E3 for the reference's supply common (U1 pin 4 and R25 / C4 are wired to the E3 line itself; R24 / C15 and the CR6 and CR8 anodes end on ground symbols, taken as the same common -- see the caveat 'Two commons, two ground symbols'). The reference output is protected by CR6 and CR8 (12 V zeners to common) and, outside the board, by the term strip inside the front panel (final-assembly R1 2 ohm, C1 82 uF, CR1, RV1, DS1 across 10V HI / LO). No A5 test point sits on a supply line.",
